# cloak/noble: the Long noble cloak (OUTER, P2b wave 2; kings, the royal guard, captains): to the ankles, its edges and
# hem trimmed in the person's trim metal (gilt by default), lined in the accent colour (the lining shows wherever the
# inside of the cloak does), a standing collar behind the neck; the drapes and the chain are cloak/noble_front.
# It hangs behind the body (over it facing up) and rides the hang channel, so every clip's hang key moves it with the
# skirts: the hem sways by whole rows on the front and back walks (sway 7), kicks back on the side walk's contact frames
# (wide), flies in the run (flare), folds on a seat (sit) or a saddle (ride), pools on the ground (kneel, floor) and lies spread
# under a corpse (lie). 20 px across, 16 px deep at most, so the cloaked look's atlases stay near B10's budgets.
# Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# (LADDER-ARMOUR polish i3) the back (facing U) at T5+ redrawn (the panel: "a symmetrical bell of a cloak, the helm a drum on
# it, no neck, hair or legs: a trash can"): hung from the shoulders, narrower than the pauldrons, the hem above the calves
# so the legs and boots read, folds lit from the top left. T5 a square gilt hem and the escutcheon; T6 a shoulder mantle,
# a pointed hem and the star; the Mythic WHITE (linen) with a sun and a burning hem (glow) -- its own palette, never T5's red.
# Every other Mythic view is its view recoloured white with the hem trim in ember (V W X Z linen, ! : ^ glow).
# (LADDER-ARMOUR polish i3) the T3 / T4 backs (facing U) hung higher and slimmer: three rows shorter above the hem and a
# pixel in on each side, so the calves and boots read below it (the panel: "no legs: a trash can").
# (LADDER-ARMOUR alloys i1) the Mythic back (U) given dark structure (the owner: "a glowing white-cream slab with no
# dark values"): T6's shoulder mantle in the crimson-black cloak with a gilt hem, the white cloak in deep folds
# (step-1 troughs, the right third in shadow), the gilt sun burning at its heart, a crimson-black band over the burning hem.
# (LADDER-ARMOUR alloys i2) the Mythic cloak in its own crimson-black (cloak slot, cloakColor 480A14) with the gilt
# and ember hem, not linen white (the panel: "a bright white and gold mass", "white slab"): the dark mass carries the
# Mythic's value structure, white is left to the edge glints.
# (LADDER-ARMOUR alloys i2) the T5 back redrawn as a drape (the panel: "a big rectangle with 1 px gold stripes: a crate or
# post box"): folds fan from the collar to a scalloped gilt hem, lit on the left, the right third in shade, deep troughs
# low down; the escutcheon smaller and high under the collar; no gilt stripes down the sides.
# (LADDER-ARMOUR alloys i3) the T6 mantle top facing U in folds (lit ridges, a shadow trough per fold), not a flat
# blue plane (the style lens: "T6 U reads as a flat blue slab with a white rim").
use person
body adult
role cloak noble
layer cloakBack
anchor neck
keys hang
sway 7
legend Q cloak 0
legend R cloak 1
legend S cloak 2
legend T cloak 3
legend U cloak 4
legend k device 1
legend l device 2
legend F device 3
legend V linen 0
legend W linen 1
legend X linen 2
legend Z linen 3
legend ! glow 2
legend : glow 3
legend ^ glow 4

